Shock:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the face, agenesis of lateral incisor, bilateral cleft lip, bilateral cleft palate, cleft soft palate\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification\n\nPancreatic Acute Inflammation vs Ruptured Ovarian Cyst with Hemoperitoneum:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the face, agenesis of lateral incisor, autosomal dominant inheritance, bilateral cleft lip, bilateral cleft palate\n  Favours second: abdominal bloating, abdominal pain, abnormal vaginal bleeding, dizziness, feeling of fullness in the abdomen\n\nEctopic Pregnancy vs Pelvic Inflammatory Disease with Septic Shock:\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, breast tenderness, collapse, diarrhea, fainting\n  Favours second: chills, fever, foul-smelling vaginal discharge, lower abdominal pain, nausea and vomiting\n\nEctopic Pregnancy vs Ruptured Ovarian Cyst with Hemoperitoneum:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification\n  Favours second: abdominal bloating, abnormal vaginal bleeding, dizziness, feeling of fullness in the abdomen, fever\n\nPelvic Inflammatory Disease with Septic Shock vs Ruptured Ovarian Cyst with Hemoperitoneum:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification\n  Favours second: abdominal bloating, abdominal pain, abnormal vaginal bleeding, dizziness, feeling of fullness in the abdomen\n\nRelated to Pancreatic Acute Inflammation: disease of orbital part of eye adnexa, orbital cellulitis, orbital osteomyelitis\n\nRelated to Ectopic Pregnancy: abdominal ectopic pregnancy, female reproductive system disease, ovarian ectopic pregnancy\n\nRelated to Pelvic Inflammatory Disease with Septic Shock: abdominal and pelvic